// Go workspace tying the three reference modules together so nekton can reuse
// plankton's shared `core` (canonicalization, hashing, DSSE) while staying its own module.
// Dependency direction is one-way: nekton -> plankton (never the reverse). See
// docs/M1-cutlist.md and DECISIONS §2. A post-v1 step promotes `core` to a neutral module.
go 1.22

use (
	./reference
	./nekton/reference
	./kton/reference
)
